---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About — WC2026 Prediction Tracker"
  description="How this World Cup 2026 prediction tracker works, how verdicts are scored, and the role of AI in building and maintaining it."
>

  <section style="padding-top:2.5rem;max-width:680px;">

    <p class="section-label" style="margin-bottom:0.75rem;">About this site</p>

    <h1
      style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,4rem);font-weight:800;letter-spacing:0.01em;text-transform:uppercase;line-height:0.95;color:var(--color-text);margin-bottom:1.5rem;"
    >
      One person's calls.<br />No wriggle room.
    </h1>

    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1.5rem;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--color-text);opacity:0.85;">

      <p>
        This is a running log of my World Cup 2026 predictions, tracked honestly against the actual results as they come in.
        Every call was made before kick-off. Nothing gets rewritten after the fact.
        The accuracy numbers you see are computed automatically from the raw data, not hand-picked.
      </p>

      <p>
        The idea is simple: make a prediction, log the reasoning, see if you were right, and learn something about where your thinking is sharp and where it is not.
        Right now the meta-lesson is already clear — I am pretty good at picking who wins, and less good at picking by how much.
        Scoreline discipline is the thing to fix.
      </p>

    </div>

    <!-- Divider -->
    <hr class="divider" style="margin:2rem 0;" />

    <!-- How scoring works -->
    <h2
      style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text);margin-bottom:1rem;"
    >
      How the scoring works
    </h2>

    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.6rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      {[
        { badge: 'badge-exact',   label: 'EXACT',   desc: 'Predicted the correct scoreline — the right result and the right goals.' },
        { badge: 'badge-correct', label: 'CORRECT', desc: 'Got the right outcome (win/draw/loss) but the scoreline was off.' },
        { badge: 'badge-miss',    label: 'MISS',    desc: 'Wrong outcome. The result went the other way.' },
        { badge: 'badge-pending', label: 'PENDING', desc: "Match hasn't been played yet. Prediction is locked in, result is not." },
      ].map(({ badge, label, desc }) => (
        <div
          style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:0.875rem;background-color:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:6px;padding:0.75rem 1rem;"
        >
          <span class={`badge ${badge}`} style="margin-top:2px;flex-shrink:0;">{label}</span>
          <span style="font-size:0.84rem;color:var(--color-text);opacity:0.8;line-height:1.6;">{desc}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p style="font-size:0.84rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--color-text);opacity:0.75;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      Scorer calls are tracked separately — <span class="badge badge-hit">HIT</span> if the named player scored,
      <span class="badge badge-assist">ASSIST</span> if they were directly involved but did not score,
      <span class="badge badge-miss">MISS</span> if they had no involvement.
      Some calls are flagged as "goal or assist" — those count as a HIT on either.
    </p>

    <hr class="divider" style="margin:2rem 0;" />

    <!-- Prediction types -->
    <h2
      style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text);margin-bottom:1rem;"
    >
      Prediction types
    </h2>

    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.6rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
      {[
        { badge: 'predtype-mismatch',        label: 'Mismatch',      desc: 'Clear quality gap. A multi-goal margin is on the table.' },
        { badge: 'predtype-favourite-tight', label: 'Fav (tight)',   desc: 'One side is better but the game will be close. Backing a narrow win.' },
        { badge: 'predtype-draw',            label: 'Draw call',     desc: 'Genuinely even game. The draw is the highest-probability single outcome.' },
        { badge: 'predtype-rule-bend',       label: 'Rule bend',     desc: 'Going against the method slightly. Noted explicitly and explained.' },
      ].map(({ badge, label, desc }) => (
        <div
          style="display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:0.875rem;background-color:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-border);border-radius:6px;padding:0.75rem 1rem;"
        >
          <span class={`badge ${badge}`} style="margin-top:2px;flex-shrink:0;border-width:1px;">{label}</span>
          <span style="font-size:0.84rem;color:var(--color-text);opacity:0.8;line-height:1.6;">{desc}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <hr class="divider" style="margin:2rem 0;" />

    <!-- AI section -->
    <h2
      style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text);margin-bottom:1rem;"
    >
      The role of AI
    </h2>

    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1rem;font-size:0.88rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--color-text);opacity:0.85;">
      <p>
        The predictions are mine. The reasoning is mine. I watch the football, read the team news, and make the call before kick-off.
      </p>
      <p>
        What AI handles is everything else: building and maintaining this site, logging results as they come in, computing the verdicts, keeping the accuracy dashboard up to date, and making sure nothing slips through the cracks. The daily workflow is: verified result comes in, I describe it in plain English to Claude Code, it finds the right match in the data file and fills in the actual score and scorers, then rebuilds and deploys automatically via Netlify.
      </p>
      <p>
        The AI also cross-checks results across multiple sources (ESPN, FOX Sports, NBC Sports) before logging anything, and will not update a match until the full-time whistle is confirmed. That matters because fast-moving live feeds occasionally get things wrong in the first few minutes after a goal or at the final whistle.
      </p>
      <p style="color:var(--color-muted);">
        Built with Astro, Tailwind CSS v4, and TypeScript. Deployed on Netlify. All verdicts derived from a single TypeScript data file — nothing hardcoded.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="divider" style="margin:2rem 0;" />

    <!-- Back link -->
    <a
      href="/"
      style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;font-size:0.82rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--color-accent);text-decoration:none;letter-spacing:0.04em;"
    >
      <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none">
        <path d="M9 2L4 7L9 12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>
      Back to predictions
    </a>

  </section>

</Layout>
